### Explanation
The code is vulnerable to insecure deserialization (CWE-502) because it uses `ObjectInputStream.readObject()` to deserialize untrusted byte data. An attacker could craft a malicious byte stream containing a serialized object that executes arbitrary code upon deserialization, leading to remote code execution (RCE) or other security issues.

### Fixed code
```java
import java.io.*;

public class InvoiceService {
    public Invoice processInvoice(byte[] invoiceBytes) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        ByteArrayInputStream bis = new ByteArrayInputStream(invoiceBytes);
        ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(bis);
        ois.setObjectInputFilter((desc, clazz, array) -> {
            // Allow only the expected class and its subclasses
            if (clazz == null || clazz == Invoice.class || clazz.isAssignableFrom(Invoice.class)) {
                return ObjectInputFilter.Status.ALLOW;
            }
            return ObjectInputFilter.Status.REJECT;
        });
        Invoice invoice = (Invoice) ois.readObject();
        ois.close();
        invoice.calculateTotal();
        invoice.applyDiscounts();
        return invoice;
    }
}
```

